pt":"Today I stopped by for an oyster po'boy and gumbo. Unfortunately, they were out of oysters and po'boy bread, so I opted for the shrimp on toast with gumbo. I must say, the food was really good! It's always those corner store places that have some of the best food. The shrimp sandwich was full of perfectly fried and battered shrimp. I like that they do not over batter the shrimp. The gumbo was excellent for gumbo that's not \"your mama's.\" Deep roux, full of meat, and flavorful. I really enjoyed both. Customer service was fine! Parking is a little weird."},{"business_id":"yWrk4Ayxxuq95120ygE4ow","review_id":"UMQmMwh7fc_-F4SVdW-lnw","date":"2009-01-14T17:11:00","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9043660759925842,"text_excerpt":"Order your fried pork chop po' boy, and you'll know why its called Riteway. The Porkchops were huge, double layered in the center of the sandwich, tasty batter and $6 to boot. Great flaky bread that made an army of crumbs, probably from Gendusa's, and a tasty fry batter. Favorite part for me is half way through eating, when I hit bone...I don't know why, but a bone-in pork chop Po Boy is always a special treat...it requires some work, but this kind of work I don't mind. Riteway has all the standards, including the french-fry Po Boy, which can't be ordered near the Quarter anymore as the places that still sell them there seem to have forgot that a fried potato Po Boy is really to be sold a..."},{"business_id":"yWrk4Ayxxuq95120ygE4ow","review_id":"CvUIK4hK82E2V5I8y_1vrg","date":"2015-05-04T00:01:43","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.8572397232055664,"text_excerpt":"I really like the gumbo! Sooooo good and hits the spot!!!!! The owners are very nice!!!!!!"}],"visual":[{"business_id":"yWrk4Ayxxuq95120ygE4ow","photo_id":"8Y_FDMQu8jHiLHJGbBqfSQ","label":"menu","image_url":"/photos/8Y_FDMQu8jHiLHJGbBqfSQ.jpg","visual_representativeness":1.0000001192092896}]},"notebook_case":null}
